WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:08.223
If one glomerulus spreads its output all over the cortex, is the chemistry lost?

2
00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:12.587
First, what does similar mean for a whole population of neurons?

3
00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:19.310
Record many piriform neurons while a mouse smells odour A. Write down each neuron's

4
00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:20.310
response.

5
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.540
This one fired. That one did not.

6
00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:25.480
A third fired a little.

7
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.200
That list is A's population pattern.

8
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:34.770
Do the same for odour B. Two odours are represented similarly if many of the same

9
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.190
neurons respond to both.

10
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.680
Real analyses correlate the responses of many neurons.

11
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.120
That is a related measure, but not the same number.

12
00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:51.073
Now the wiring. Tracing found that each piriform neuron gets input from several

13
00:00:51.073 --> 00:00:52.893
glomeruli spread across the bulb.

14
00:00:53.883 --> 00:00:57.063
Driving one glomerulus did not make the cells fire.

15
00:00:57.983 --> 00:01:02.303
In this simple model, a neuron fires only when enough inputs are active together.

16
00:01:03.383 --> 00:01:06.203
Nothing about the neuron's position enters the model.

17
00:01:07.183 --> 00:01:12.983
Here is a toy. Each neuron listens to two glomeruli and fires only if both are

18
00:01:12.983 --> 00:01:15.283
active. Wiring is random.

19
00:01:16.317 --> 00:01:18.597
Odour A activates ten glomeruli.

20
00:01:19.477 --> 00:01:23.397
A related ester, B, also activates ten, and shares six with A.

21
00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.677
An unrelated amine, C, shares none.

22
00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:30.450
Any pair of A's glomeruli can feed a neuron.

23
00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:34.750
Those neurons respond to A. The pairs are counted on screen.

24
00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:37.820
Which of them also respond to B?

25
00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:42.440
Only neurons whose two inputs both sit among the six shared glomeruli.

26
00:01:43.483 --> 00:01:44.683
Pause and predict.

27
00:01:45.663 --> 00:01:48.263
The odours share sixty percent of their glomeruli.

28
00:01:49.163 --> 00:01:51.723
What share of A's neurons also respond to B?

29
00:01:57.683 --> 00:01:59.363
About one third, on average.

30
00:02:00.283 --> 00:02:04.343
The odours share most of their glomeruli, but only a third of their responsive

31
00:02:04.343 --> 00:02:05.343
neurons.

32
00:02:05.917 --> 00:02:10.597
And for C, no A neuron responds at all, because no glomeruli are shared.

33
00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:12.847
Two results follow.

34
00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:15.647
B is still far more like A than C is.

35
00:02:16.507 --> 00:02:18.047
The order of similarity survives.

36
00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:20.707
But the overlap has shrunk.

37
00:02:21.647 --> 00:02:26.307
Both of a neuron's inputs must be shared, so six tenths times five ninths gives one

38
00:02:26.307 --> 00:02:27.307
third.

39
00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:32.070
Where the neurons sit never entered the calculation.

40
00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:38.520
A larger toy, with a thousand glomeruli and twenty inputs per neuron, gives the same

41
00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:39.520
two results.

42
00:02:40.233 --> 00:02:41.533
The order is kept.

43
00:02:42.733 --> 00:02:44.793
Related odours become less alike, not more.

44
00:02:45.733 --> 00:02:48.873
So in this model, where a neuron sits does not matter.

45
00:02:49.733 --> 00:02:51.153
Which glomeruli feed it does.

46
00:02:53.333 --> 00:02:55.273
So here is a test for real data.

47
00:02:56.133 --> 00:03:00.853
If piriform worked like this model, related odours should be less alike there, not

48
00:03:00.853 --> 00:03:01.853
more.

49
00:03:02.117 --> 00:03:07.537
In this model, random wiring keeps the expected order of likeness, but makes related

50
00:03:07.537 --> 00:03:08.557
odours less alike.

51
00:03:09.517 --> 00:03:11.657
Anything tighter needs more than this model.
